      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "scd2",
          "text": "Inspections are an important part of commercial truck safety. Missing an inspection or a failed inspection is a sign that the trucking company acted negligently in maintaining the safety of their vehicles. Inspection reports can shed light on how safe the truck was at the time of the accident.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bcd5",
      "style": "h4",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "scd4",
          "text": "Alcohol and Drug Testing Results",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bcd7",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "scd6",
          "text": "After a truck accident, police officials may perform an alcohol or drug test on the truck driver to determine if intoxication played a role in the crash. Your attorney will need to obtain copies of these results, as well as any other past failed drug tests.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
